    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2503.17594v1</id>
    <title>A new tail bound for the sum of bounded independent random variables</title>
    <updated>2025-03-22T00:44:51Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.17594v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2503.17594v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>We construct a new tail bound for the sum of independent random variables for situations in which the expected value of the sum is known and each random variable lies within a specified interval, which may be different for each variable. This new bound can be computed by solving a two-dimensional convex optimization problem. Simulations demonstrate that the new bound is often substantially tighter than Hoeffding's inequality for cases in which both bounds are applicable.</summary>
    <category term="math.PR" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <category term="math.ST" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
